caps.find(c=>c.id==='PLN-13').layers.actualOutput='PARTIAL';
set('PLN-14','COMPLETE','A delay event names the ACTIVITIES it hit, canonically (migration 0325). It has carried a WBS code as free text since it was introduced — a label that drifts the first time somebody renumbers a package, and a link no query can follow, which is not a basis for a contractual instrument. That column stays as the note it always was and is deliberately not migrated: nobody can map free text onto an activity id after the fact, and guessing would manufacture the lineage this exists to make real. TWO FACTS ARE KEPT APART because an EOT dispute is precisely the confusion of them: CLAIMED is how long the event lasted, a fact about the world; IMPACT is how many working days completion actually moved, a fact about the plan. A ten-day storm on an activity with float moves completion by less, or by nothing. A contractor claims the first, an employer grants the second, and a system reporting only one has taken a side. The impact is derived by running the SAME CPM twice — as planned, and with the delay inserted — and diffing the finishes, so the project has one answer to “when does this finish” rather than a bespoke delay calculator beside the planner. Counted in WORKING days under the project’s calendar (PLN-03): a figure in calendar days is indefensible the moment the contract is not, and a storm over a weekend nobody was going to work delayed nothing. ‘Absorbed by float’ is a real verdict rather than a failure to reach one. CONCURRENCY IS NAMED AND NEVER APPORTIONED — an overlapping delay is reported with its cause and left there, because whether it reduces liability is a question of contract and law decided by people, and halving a figure on that basis would be inventing a legal position inside arithmetic. The ASSESSMENT is a separate, recorded act: a figure, a name and a moment, stored beside the derived impact and never instead of it, so a number submitted against the plan as it then stood survives the plan moving. Zero is accepted — it is the commonest honest answer. Assessing carries `projects.delay.assess`, which a Planning Engineer holds and which does not carry the commercial decision on the claim.','Auth-ON browser and HTTP proof on a critical chain under a Gulf calendar: a delay naming no activity the programme holds reports UNKNOWN rather than a confident figure; named on the critical path, three claimed days read as three working days of completion lost, 2026-03-16 → 2026-03-19, stepping over the weekend; the same three-day event moved onto an activity with slack reads ABSORBED_BY_FLOAT with completion unmoved; a concurrent contractor-caused delay is named with its cause and changes the figure by nothing; an assessment records a figure, a name and a moment and moves the event to `analysed`; a negative figure and a missing one are refused; and stretching the critical activity afterwards changes the DERIVED impact while the submitted figure stands. Twelve domain rules cover the edges, including a programme that cannot be placed at all. The recovery-proposal criterion is closed in iteration 16: a delay assessment now hands off EXPLICITLY to a recovery proposal that carries canonical lineage back to this delay and to the assessment that justified it, frozen at the hand-off — proven Auth-ON from assessment to accepted programme. The hand-off is a button somebody presses rather than an automatic re-plan, which is a design decision recorded in the Wave 3 report and not a gap. STILL OPEN: a delay reaches nobody who is not looking at the screen, which is the same notification gap five other rows carry.','handoff');
for (const layer of ['domain','persistence','api','permissions','ui','browser','handoff']) caps.find(c=>c.id==='PLN-14').layers[layer]='COMPLETE';
caps.find(c=>c.id==='PLN-14').layers.actualOutput='PARTIAL';
set('PLN-15','COMPLETE','The chain runs end to end and each link is a stored row: delay event → derived impact → recorded assessment → EXPLICIT prepare-recovery hand-off → recovery proposal → review → acceptance → the programme moves. A RECOVERY PROPOSAL IS A SCENARIO: stored beside the programme, changing not one stored date, and becoming current only through a governed acceptance — a re-plan that quietly became the plan is how a project’s dates stop meaning anything, because nobody can say when they were last agreed to. The hand-off is DELIBERATELY EXPLICIT: an assessment that silently launched a re-plan would produce a proposal nobody asked for against a programme nobody agreed to move, and the planner who must defend the recovery would not have chosen its starting point. It refuses a delay nobody has assessed — there is nothing to be a recovery OF — and a delay belonging to another project. The proposal carries canonical lineage to the delay AND to the assessed impact, frozen at the hand-off so a later re-assessment cannot rewrite what it was prepared against; the two are read side by side and are allowed to disagree, because “assessed at 3 days lost, this recovers 8” is two assessments of two different things. It uses the same calendar, the same dependency network and the same CPM as the programme. What it is judged on is the COMPARISON — current finish, proposed finish, working days recovered under the project’s calendar — never the proposal’s own finish date: zero says the re-plan found nothing, and a NEGATIVE figure says the scenario is worse than what it would replace, which is exactly the one nobody should accept by reflex and the one a finish date alone hides. Acceptance now also checks the PLANNING BASIS (migration 0326): a fingerprint of every input the solver consumed — each task’s dates and authored duration, the dependency edges, the calendar named — is taken at run time and compared at acceptance, so a programme that moved underneath a proposal is caught even when every task id still matches. The previous guard compared the task SET alone and passed silently on a changed duration, date, edge or calendar.','Auth-ON browser and HTTP proof of the whole chain: the hand-off is refused for an unassessed delay and offered only once an assessment exists; a prepared proposal carries `sourceDelayId` and the frozen assessed impact and a 64-character basis fingerprint; preparing one moves not a single stored date; the comparison reports current 2026-03-24, the proposed finish, and 8 WORKING days recovered under a Gulf calendar (not the 12 calendar days between them); discarding leaves the programme untouched and a discarded proposal cannot then be accepted (409); extending one activity’s duration — no task added or removed — is caught at acceptance as a changed planning basis (409) with the programme unmoved; acceptance moves the programme to exactly the proposed finish and the same proposal cannot be accepted twice. Under a LIVE VERIFIER: a Planning Engineer assesses the delay, prepares the recovery and reads what it would recover, and is REFUSED the acceptance (403) with nothing moved; a stranger is refused the scenario, the hand-off and the acceptance alike (403), server-side rather than by a hidden button; and the Project Manager accepts it and the programme moves. STILL OPEN: acceptance does not re-baseline — the baseline and the actuals are deliberately left exactly as they were, so a recovered programme and the baseline it is measured against diverge until somebody re-baselines on purpose; and a proposal reaches nobody who is not looking at the screen.','browser');
