 currentBehavior:'A rate-build-up component could be priced from a pre-award RFQ quote, and when that RFQ was awarded a subscriber restamped every component sourced from it to the awarded amount. SUP-14 retired the award it listened for: a purchase order is no longer raised from a quote header, so `procurement.rfq.awarded` has no producer. A governed award CANNOT take its place without inventing a mapping — an `aura_tendering_estimate_sources` row records the legacy RFQ QUOTE a component was priced from, carries no material and no requisition line, and the old restamp set EVERY component on an RFQ to a SINGLE amount, so feeding it a whole-offer total would write one supplier’s entire offer onto each component as a unit cost. The subscriber therefore no longer restamps and instead WARNS, naming the RFQ and how many components on how many tenders are affected — chosen over a silent subscriber, which would look exactly like a feature that works. Bid-time SOURCING itself is unaffected; only the award-time restamp is.',
