 currentBehavior:'Every path that turns an amount into money now refuses rather than invents. AP and AR invoice creation resolve through a strict authority AT THE DOCUMENT’S OWN DATE — the supplier’s invoice date, the customer’s issue date — and an ungoverned currency is refused before the command bus is entered, so nothing is left behind: no row, no line, no outbox event, no journal. The domain carries the same invariant inside the transaction, where a foreign-currency invoice can no longer be constructed without a rate at all; it used to default a missing rate to 1. Base-to-base is an explicit IDENTITY needing no governed row, so an ordinary AED invoice is never refused for want of an AED:AED rate. Both revaluations resolve the CURRENT rate at the revaluation date rather than at today, so a closed period no longer moves when a later rate is registered; exposure that cannot be valued is reported as unresolved and the revaluation refuses to post, where it previously fell back to the booked rate, reported a gain/loss of zero and posted nothing — indistinguishable from a position that had genuinely not moved. The booked rate is never re-resolved: a correction to the register does not restate a document. Each booked invoice records WHICH governed rate valued it — effective date, source, and the aura_exchange_rates row id (migration 0348) — and legacy rows are left NULL rather than backfilled, because NULL is the honest value. The currency boundary is one policy in @aura/shared asked by the DTO, the domain and the FX authority alike, with the runtime list deriving the type so they cannot drift.',
